---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    participant Page as Admin sites page<br/>/admin/sites
    participant Actions as Server actions<br/>utils/supabase/queries.ts
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL

    Note over Admin,DB: Covers US 2.0.2. /admin/sites exists but has no Add Site flow. All add steps are Proposed.<br/>ProtectedRoute requireAdmin hides the page in the browser only. It reads user_metadata, so it is not a security check.

    Admin->>Page: Select "Add Site" (Proposed)
    activate Page
    Page->>Actions: getUnmatchedKmlSites() (Proposed, AT6)
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: Check session and Admin role on server (Proposed)
    Actions->>DB: Read kml_sites rows (loaded by US 6.0.1)<br/>that no sites_pa.source_feature_id references
    activate DB
    DB-->>Actions: Suggested Sites with boundaries
    deactivate DB
    Actions-->>Page: Suggestions
    deactivate Actions
    Page-->>Admin: Show suggestions on a map

    Admin->>Page: Select a boundary (AT1), enter name and county
    Page->>Actions: findSitesWithName(name) (Proposed)
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: Check session and Admin role on server (Proposed)
    Actions->>DB: Read sites_pa rows with the same name,<br/>active and inactive
    activate DB
    DB-->>Actions: Matching Sites
    deactivate DB
    Actions-->>Page: Matching Sites
    deactivate Actions
    opt A Site with the same name exists (AT2)
        Page-->>Admin: Show a possible-duplicate warning before save
    end

    Admin->>Page: Select Save
    Page->>Page: Check required fields, for example name
    alt A required field is empty (AT3)
        Page-->>Admin: Block creation and highlight the empty fields
    else Required fields are filled
        Page->>Actions: createSite(name, county, boundary) (Proposed)
        activate Actions
        Actions->>Actions: Check session and Admin role on server
        alt Caller is not an Admin, for example a Steward<br/>who sends the request directly (AT4)
            Actions-->>Page: Refuse (403), no Site created
            Page-->>Admin: Show "Only an Admin can add a Site"
        else Caller is an Admin
            Actions->>Actions: Check required fields again (AT3)
            Actions->>DB: Insert sites_pa row (is_active = true) with the boundary.<br/>If it is a suggestion, also set source_feature_id
            activate DB
            alt Insert fails
                DB-->>Actions: Error
                Actions-->>Page: Error, nothing saved
                Page-->>Admin: Show the error and keep the form
            else Insert done
                DB-->>Actions: New Site id
                Actions-->>Page: New Site
                Page-->>Admin: Show the new Site in the list
            end
            deactivate DB
        end
        deactivate Actions
    end
    deactivate Page

    Note over Admin,DB: A new Site is active by default (US 2.0.3 AT5). getSitesOnline reads active Sites, so the new Site<br/>shows in Site search (AT5). Open question: can the Admin save after the duplicate warning?<br/>namesite is UNIQUE in the local schema copy (webapp/supabase/migrations).<br/>Open question: load the KML into a table or read the file each time. kml_sites is the proposed option (see US 6.0.1).
